---
title: "UML-Style State Machine — AIOS Operating and Recovery Modes"
---
%% Proposed three-resource control with independent gates
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Starting
  Starting --> OBSERVE_ONLY: startup complete [required services healthy] / keep control disabled
  Starting --> FALLBACK: [validation or required-service check fails]
  OBSERVE_ONLY --> WARNING: [stale, uncertain, or pressure condition detected]
  WARNING --> OBSERVE_ONLY: [freshness and health checks pass]
  OBSERVE_ONLY --> RESOURCE_CONTROL: [host-local policy, resource capability, and safety gates pass]
  RESOURCE_CONTROL --> OBSERVE_ONLY: [policy disables control or a health gate fails]
  WARNING --> FALLBACK: [watchdog timeout or unsafe condition]
  OBSERVE_ONLY --> FALLBACK: [unsafe input or watchdog failure]
  RESOURCE_CONTROL --> FALLBACK: [IPC, actuator, or watchdog fault]
  FALLBACK --> RECOVERY_CHECK: recovery begins after service restart
  RECOVERY_CHECK --> OBSERVE_ONLY: [checks pass] / keep active control disabled
  RECOVERY_CHECK --> FALLBACK: [any recovery check fails]
  note right of RESOURCE_CONTROL
    One bounded action per request: cpu.weight, memory.high, or supported io.weight / io.max.
    Each resource has an independent capability and safety gate. memory.max and process termination are excluded.
  end note
  note right of FALLBACK
    Block new AI writes. Restore a captured value only for a verified AIOS-owned target.
    If safe rollback fails, stay fail-closed and report degraded mode.
  end note
  note left of OBSERVE_ONLY
    Default mode. Viewers can read status only.
    The dashboard cannot change mode or authorize actions.
  end note
